   "system": {
    "source_reference": {
     "source": "core_rulebook",
     "page": 129
    },
    "description": "<ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">You are well-known, but not for the right reasons. Characters who do not know you personally always assume that those around you will perish or meet bad ends, even if you survive to spread your ill fortune further.</span></p><p></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">When you make a check to dispel someone’s false preconceptions (such as a Courtesy [Void] check to get someone to question their decision or a Command [Void] check to get someone to see the pointlessness of their position), you must choose and reroll two dice containing (su)</span><span class=\"fontstyle3\"> </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">or (ex). After resolving the check, if you failed, you gain 1 Void point.</span></p></li></ul>",
    "parent_id": null,
