   "system": {
    "source_reference": {
     "source": "core_rulebook",
     "page": 132
    },
    "description": "<ul><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">You have a dark secret that, if exposed, could bring ruin upon your house and disgrace your ancestors and descendants alike. If the details of this secret become public, your glory value decreases dramatically, as if you had lost staked glory (by 10 to 20). Depending on the secret, your status value might also decrease considerably (by 5 to 10), as if you had lost staked status.</span></p><p></p></li><li><p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">After performing a check to assert your will over yourself or others (such as a Command [Void] check to order troops to fight to the bitter end or a Meditation [Void] check to find inner peace), you receive 3 strife. If this is the first time this has occurred this scene, gain 1 Void point.</span></p></li></ul>",
    "parent_id": null,
